# TASK-056 — Nav.diff
# Guard pattern: {#if leading} — NO CHANGES REQUIRED

## SCOPE
Nav.svelte lines 43-46 (leading guard) and line 72 (item.icon render)

## ANALYSIS

### Line 43-46: {#if leading} guard
```svelte
{#if leading}
    <span class="nav-leading">
        {@render leading()}
    </span>
{/if}
```

**Verdict: CORRECT — no changes needed.**

After TopAppBar.svelte fix:
- When showBack=true: Nav receives `leading={backBtn}` → snippet reference is valid → renders ✓
- When showBack=false: Nav instance has NO `leading` prop → defaults to `undefined` → `{#if undefined}` = falsy → does NOT render ✓
- HMR scenario: Nav instances are never toggled in-place (the `{#if showBack}` in TopAppBar mounts/unmounts entire Nav). No stale snippet references reach this guard.

### Line 72: {#snippet item.icon()} render
```svelte
{@render item.icon()}
```

**Verdict: SAFE — no changes needed.**

- New BottomNav always provides valid snippet references (walletIcon, historyIcon)
- These snippet references are defined as {#snippet} blocks and never become undefined
- The {#each} loop only iterates over pre-defined items with guaranteed icon properties

### POTENTIAL EDGE CASE (not triggered in current architecture)
If items were externally sourced with potentially missing `icon`, a guard like `{#if item.icon}{@render item.icon()}{/if}` would be needed.
But since BottomNav is the sole consumer and always provides icon snippets, this is not required.
